<title>ITALY: Italy lira weakens past ERM central parity vs mark.</title>
<headline>Italy lira weakens past ERM central parity vs mark.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian lira weakened past its central parity of 990 per mark in the European exchange rate mechanism in the European afternoon.</p>
<p>By 1440 GMT, the Italian currency was quoted at 990.95/1.25 per mark compared with 985.20 early in European trade.</p>
<p>Dealers said the Italian currency, which has been holding fairly steady above the central ERM rate in recent days, was weakening alongside other European currencies like the French franc.</p>
</text>
